  "texts": {
    "preamble": "K.V.Mahesh vs Secretary To Government on 16 April, 2024 Author: D.Bharatha Chakravarthy Bench: D.Bharatha Chakravarthy W.P. In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 16.04.2024 Coram The Hon'Ble Mr Justice D.Bharatha Chakravarthy W.P.No.9364 of 2024 K.V.Mahesh ... Pe -Versus- 1.Secretary to Government, Health and Family Welfare Department, Secretariat, Chennai 600 009. 2.The Commissioner, Food Safety and Drug Administrative Department , Anna Salai, Chennai 600 006. 3.The Designated Officer, Food Safety and Drug Administrative Department, Gandhi Road, Tanjore. 4.The Designated Officer, Food safety and Drug Administrative Department, Sadhanandhapuram, Pudukottai 622 001. ... Re Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of I Writ of Mandamus directing the respondents to consider the representatio the petitioner dated 25.01.2024 and consequently directing the responden pay additional charge allowance for working as additional charge food sa officer to Kumbakkonam Block, Tanjore District from 06.09.2018 to https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 1 of 4 W 26.02.2021 and Gantharvakottai Block, Pudhukottai District from 03.09.20 to 09.11.2023. K.V.Mahesh vs Secretary To Government on 16 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/68709911/ 1 For Petitioner : Mr.U.Jugal Kumar For Respondents : Mr.M.Bindhran, Additional Government Pleade Order 2. When the matter came up for hearing, the learned Additional Government Pleader appearing on behalf of the respondents would place the proceedings of the Commissioner of Food Safety and Drug Administration dated 03.04.2024. As per the said proceedings, it is stated that the Food Safety Officers menioned in the enclosure to the said proceedings were already sanctioned with an additional charge allowance at the rate mentioned therein. For various periods, all the entitled officers have been sanctioned and the name of the petitioner finds place in the annexure. 3 . I n v i e w t h e r e o f , t h e g r i e v a n c e o f t h e p e t i t i o n e r h a s b e e n r e d r e s s e d b y https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 2 of 4 the said proceedings dated 03.04.2024.",
    "facts": "This Writ Petition is filed to consider the representation of the petitioner and consequently to direct the respondents to pay the additional charge allowance for the petitioner, who is working as an additional charge Food Safety Officer.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
